    size: 6-9 rows x 8-10 cols
    position: each margin (frame edge to grid edge) >= 1; asymmetric placement allowed
    interior: all cells inside frame are bg(0) in input
  markers:
    color: always 5 [observed]; exactly 2 foreground colors total
    count: 2-4 pixels scattered inside the frame interior
    bbox: 2-4 rows x 2-4 cols; strictly inside frame (each gap from marker bbox edge to frame edge >= 1)
    density: markers are sparse within their bbox (only 0 and marker_color present)
    constraint: frame_color pixel count >> marker_color pixel count (frame is the majority fg color)
  transform:
    rule: fill all bg cells strictly inside the frame with frame_color, EXCEPT cells within the marker bbox which are left unchanged
    result: frame interior becomes solid frame_color with a rectangular "window" at marker bbox preserving original content

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims (H 8-13, W 11-12) and frame bbox with each margin >= 1, frame 6-9 x 8-10
    2. Pick marker bbox strictly inside frame (each gap >= 1), size 2-4 x 2-4
    3. Place 2-4 marker pixels (color 5) inside marker bbox on random positions; rest of bbox stays bg
    4. Build output: frame border = 2, interior filled with 2, marker bbox region keeps its bg+marker content
    5. Derive input from output: set all interior cells that are frame_color (excluding the frame border itself) back to bg(0)
